WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:02.573
- If you don't mind my asking,

00:00:02.573 --> 00:00:03.675
I'm really curious,

00:00:03.675 --> 00:00:06.963
what made you start all this?

00:00:06.963 --> 00:00:09.163
- [Mark] I'm just
fascinated with how people

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.011
tend to willingly self-destruct.

00:00:13.011 --> 00:00:13.844
- Yeah.

00:00:13.844 --> 00:00:15.110
- [Mark] And just ruin their own lives.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.010
And I've been fascinated with that

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.460
since I realized people
were doing it, in my life.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.570
And even I do it to some extent.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.403
And it's...

00:00:26.188 --> 00:00:27.021
And the more I do it,

00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:29.731
I've done well over 2,000
of these interviews,

00:00:29.731 --> 00:00:30.564
- Mm-hm.

00:00:30.564 --> 00:00:31.397
- [Mark] The more I do it,

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.980
the more I kind of get a better
grip on what's causing it,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.270
and why people do it, and
why they can't stop doing it.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.760
- Yeah, you see patterns.
- Y-Yeah.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.000
There's certain things that certain parts

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.090
of their childhood,
usually, that have repeated

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.077
over and over and over.
- Yeah.

00:00:46.077 --> 00:00:47.420
- And that's the stem of it all.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.759
And then it just repeats
generation after generation.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.121
- Yeah, it's crazy.

00:00:52.121 --> 00:00:54.240
But that's super cool, yeah.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.220
- [Mark] And I think we all go through it.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.400
- Oh, yeah, in different ways.
- Everyone,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.233
everyone to some extent.

00:00:58.233 --> 00:00:59.810
I mean, these are maybe
the more extreme stories

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:00.870
on my channel,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.590
but everybody is struggling
with this kind of stuff.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.150
- Yeah, yeah.
- To some extent.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.130
So that's why-
- Definitely.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.800
- That's why I think it's been so popular

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.840
is because you can
relate to these stories,

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.780
even if you think you're not
a drug addict, which I'm not.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.077
Or you're not a prostitute or whatever

00:01:14.077 --> 00:01:17.859
but that self-destruction is
something that we all have.

00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:19.380
- Yeah, exactly.
- And it can be,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.210
there's so many different
ways it plays out,

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.510
whether it's, you know,
drugs or alcohol or gambling

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:29.287
or shopping or laziness or, (chuckling)

00:01:29.287 --> 00:01:32.080
or just your personalities
pushes people away or anything.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:32.913
- Yeah.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:33.900
- So.
- Exactly.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:34.917
- [Mark] So that's what got me doing it.

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.660
- That's so cool, yeah.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.860
- [Mark] All right, Scarlett.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.780
Scarlett, where are you from?

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.095
Where'd you grow up?

00:01:40.095 --> 00:01:42.300
- I was born in Oregon

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.920
but I kind of moved all
over the country as a kid.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.703
I moved to North Carolina,
Virginia, Montana,

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.643
but I mostly grew up in LA, Los Angeles.

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:55.562
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:01:55.562 --> 00:01:58.130
You had both your parents
when you were young?

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.480
- Yeah, so I was born,

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.200
my parents got divorced
when I was in kindergarten

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.530
but up until then, I don't
really remember much.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:08.010
So up until I was six,
I don't remember much.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:12.660
And then once my parents got divorced

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.660
my dad moved me and my three
siblings to California.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.040
'Cause we were all born in Oregon.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.810
And he got remarried

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.350
because he was having
an affair with my mom,

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.050
and that's what caused the divorce.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.350
And then the woman he was
having an affair with,

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.700
eventually became our
step-mom, me and my siblings.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.295
And, yeah.
(chuckling)

00:02:36.295 --> 00:02:38.295
- How would you describe your childhood?

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:40.890
- Confusing.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:41.880
Very confusing.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.650
A lot of, I was told to
a lot of different things

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:45.990
from different people.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.880
From my mom, my dad,
step-parents, friends, relatives,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.100
so, and they were all very opposite.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.520
So it was hard to just figure
out what was, you know,

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.840
what was true and who was just feeding you

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.240
the right information, yeah.

00:03:01.553 --> 00:03:02.690
- Did you finished high school?

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:03.523
- I didn't.

00:03:03.523 --> 00:03:05.520
I dropped out my junior year,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.230
because I overdosed on Xanax
in school, in history class.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.216
And then I just, I never went back.

00:03:11.216 --> 00:03:12.860
- So drugs kind of came into your life.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:13.693
At what point?

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.640
- They came into my point.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.500
I started drinking alcohol when I was 12.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.763
And right as I started, I just,

00:03:22.663 --> 00:03:24.880
it took off and it led to other things.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.660
I was offered pills first,

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.093
before I didn't smoked weed
or anything else at school.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.330
And that was when I was 13.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:36.350
I started taking Adderall and Xanax

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.400
and that really, heavily
affected my memory,

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.700
and I started noticing that.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.810
And I think my family and
friends started noticing that

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.230
and it started affecting my grades.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.480
I was a really good student.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.230
I had straight A's and then seventh grade,

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.510
everything just kind of plummeted.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.343
Yeah.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:59.742
- [Mark] So you went on
your own at what age?

00:03:59.742 --> 00:04:02.560
- I can't really say I was on my own,

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.150
but in a way, I've been
on my own, my whole life.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.370
I've always had some sort of parent figure

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.230
but they haven't always, even
if they've been in the house

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.280
they haven't always been there, you know?

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.490
Or they've left.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.520
A lot of step parents.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.040
A lot of my dad's girlfriends
were coming, then leave.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.040
Yeah.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.310
So it just caused a lot of, I think,

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.110
I didn't have stability ever.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.210
- [Mark] And how old are you?

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.043
- I'm 18.

00:04:30.043 --> 00:04:31.070
- [Mark] You're 18?
- Yeah.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.410
- [Mark] So you've been
in LA for how long?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:40.773
- I've been in LA, on and off,
for probably about 10 years.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.390
- [Mark] 10 years!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.150
So some of your family members live here?

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:45.983
- Yeah.

00:04:45.983 --> 00:04:46.816
Most of my family lives down here.

00:04:46.816 --> 00:04:47.900
My mom lives in Oregon.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.140
My siblings all live down here.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.860
My dad lives down here,

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.820
but I don't speak to my family.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.967
- [Mark] Could you tell?
- No.

00:04:55.967 --> 00:04:58.390
- [Mark] And your drug
use is kind of continued?

00:04:58.390 --> 00:04:59.920
- Yeah, it got it.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.200
It wasn't very, it was.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.860
When I started,

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.100
people attributed it to
a lot of other things.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:06.933
My parents,

00:05:06.933 --> 00:05:10.820
or my dad thought I had a
lot of mental health issues.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.070
So when I was on drugs
and I would act out,

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.220
I would be diagnosed as
bipolar, schizophrenic,

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.950
all these things, which I wasn't.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.840
But I didn't admit that I
was using all these drugs

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.180
and all this alcohol.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.170
And then it didn't really come to light

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:27.260
until I started overdosing,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.910
and my first overdose was in eighth grade.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:34.910
And then since then I've been
in rehab, on and off in jail.

00:05:35.359 --> 00:05:36.880
Yeah.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.870
- [Mark] What's your drug-
- Xanax.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.150
But I've dabbled in everything.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.100
I was on crystal for a while.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:42.933
Pretty heavy.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.810
- What kind of stuff did
you go through as a kid?

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.750
- Okay, so, the reason
my parents got divorced.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.040
My dad had an affair

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.490
and my mom ended up finding out

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.350
that it wasn't his first affair.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.700
And it was, he'd also had affairs

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.790
not only with random women,
but with her friends as well.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.050
So I found that out at a really young age

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.220
and I didn't really understand.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.330
I mean, I was six when it all happened

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:12.440
and I was probably about seven or eight

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.620
when I started getting all the, you know

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.140
rumors or information
about what was happening.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.510
And it was all, again, mixed
from my mom and my dad.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.620
This happened, this didn't happen.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.070
So again, that was confusing.

00:06:25.102 --> 00:06:27.880
But basically the woman my dad.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.950
The main woman my dad had an affair with,

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.470
he ended up marrying and leaving my mom.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.270
And then we all moved down to California,

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.130
me and my siblings.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.550
My mom stayed back in Oregon.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:40.030
So I never lived with my
mom except for up to six.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:44.100
So when I was six, I didn't live with her.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.754
So my mom stayed in Oregon.

00:06:45.754 --> 00:06:47.660
We all moved down to California

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:52.660
and my step-mom ended up.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:55.090
We ended up seeing just patterns
and behavior that, again,

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.400
I didn't realize what they
were because I was so young.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:01.300
But she had bipolar disorder
and she was an alcoholic,

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.633
had really bad depression.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.000
The first thing I noticed,
I was like, really?

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.230
I think the most,

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.200
the first very traumatic thing in my mind

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.550
when I think of my childhood,

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:15.440
is when I was woken up in
the middle of the night

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:19.370
by like, just so much noise
and I was really scared.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.610
And I opened my bedroom door,

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.250
which I showed up to my little brother

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.560
and a bunch of firemen
were running up the stairs.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.217
And one came to the door and just told me,

00:07:28.217 --> 00:07:29.050
"Go back to sleep."

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.667
And I was like, "I'm not
gonna go back to sleep.

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:33.240
"There's a bunch of firemen in my house."

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.140
But I peered off the door
and I saw my step-mom

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.430
being wheeled out in a stretcher

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.740
and there was blood everywhere.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.170
And I found out from my sister that night,

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.020
that she tried to kill
herself with scissors

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.123
when she was drunk.

00:07:48.541 --> 00:07:50.590
So that, even though I don't
remember like the whole night

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.100
and I didn't see it happen,
it was still really traumatic.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.450
And I didn't know, she was.

00:07:55.326 --> 00:07:57.100
I didn't know she had any problems,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.430
so I didn't see anything until then.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.500
And that was kind of scary
to see at a young age.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:07.060
And then I don't think she
really hit it after that.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:10.070
So once we moved from,

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:13.320
my dad moved us from
California to North Carolina,

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.153
across the country,

00:08:14.153 --> 00:08:18.630
when I was going into seventh
grade, I think I was 13.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:22.170
And that was like a huge thing,

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:26.500
that I don't think we realized
at the time how big that was.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.400
Like moving across the country, that young

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.190
and not really having a plan,
knowing nobody over there,

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.360
that's where my stepmom was from,

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.320
so she wanted to move back there.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.040
But we ended up moving there

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.773
and I got into school there.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.910
At my school in California,

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:43.830
I was, it was fine.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:44.760
I had friends, you know,

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.230
I was a normal kid and everything.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.300
And then once I got there, it was just,

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.410
I don't know what happened.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.150
But I guess, just the new kid,

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.960
but nobody talked to
me, I was just a loner.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.600
And I just had that label from
day one, for whatever reason.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.090
And I wasn't, I did
not, not talk to people.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:03.700
You know, I was friendly, I was outgoing,

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:06.030
but nobody talked to me,
nobody, for whatever reason.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.070
I don't know why.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:08.590
So for two years,

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.780
seventh and eighth grade,
I had zero friends.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.393
I ate lunch in the bathroom.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.550
It was really hard.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:18.073
And, sorry.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:23.140
During that time, a lot
of stuff was going on

00:09:24.361 --> 00:09:25.453
at my house too.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.663
Just a lot of, my stepmom was.

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:35.070
She would just come into
my room or, thank you.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.570
Or my sister's room, my older sister

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.871
and a lot of times I would hear,

00:09:40.871 --> 00:09:41.704
dad would be laying,

00:09:41.704 --> 00:09:43.820
and I would hear her going
to my older sister's room

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.250
and yell at her, for no reason.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.450
And then I would just
hear my sister crying.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:53.100
And when I always talked to her about it,

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:58.030
she didn't say much and she
would just have panic attacks.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.163
And so I think from.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:01.880
I think from a young age

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:05.900
we all just kind of
had a lot thrown on us.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.893
And so, yeah, she would
have panic attacks.

00:10:07.893 --> 00:10:11.290
I would go into her room,
try to calm her down

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.869
and it would be over nothing.

00:10:12.869 --> 00:10:14.740
She would go into her
room and yell at her,

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.203
calling her disgusting
because my sister has OCD.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.904
Calling her names,

00:10:19.904 --> 00:10:22.430
come into my room, yell at me.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.940
Call me fat, call hideous.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.390
Don't know why, I'm 13.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.270
Don't know what I'm doing,

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.420
I don't have any friends at school.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.497
And now, you know,

00:10:29.497 --> 00:10:30.820
and my dad's not doing anything.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.583
He's sitting right there watching it.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:36.900
I don't know, just, it was hard.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:41.090
And then outside of that, I,

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:42.930
my sister was in place.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:43.983
She was in theater.

00:10:45.364 --> 00:10:48.281
(lighter striking)

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:54.100
And me and my little brother
would go and watch her

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.947
at the high school, 'cause
we were in the middle school

00:10:55.947 --> 00:10:58.050
and it was connected.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.950
So, one night, we were watching the play

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:06.520
and an older boy from the high school

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.623
started talking to me.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:13.190
And he got my number and
I was really excited.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.114
I was, nobody talked to me.

00:11:15.114 --> 00:11:16.813
No guys talked to me.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.260
And here's this 18 year old.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:21.647
He was really handsome, I remember.

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:24.560
And I was really excited
to get his number.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:26.437
