00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:30.630
Like, I really don't know what to expect.

00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:31.760
And it's just really, you know

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:33.633
it's just kind of taking a toll.

00:22:33.633 --> 00:22:34.466
- [Mark] Yeah, it's almost like

00:22:34.466 --> 00:22:35.653
you need to repair it yourself.

00:22:35.653 --> 00:22:36.750
- Yeah.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.823
- [Mark] Yeah, if you can imagine that.

00:22:38.823 --> 00:22:41.532
- If yeah.
- [Mark] Then love yourself

00:22:41.532 --> 00:22:45.340
and almost re rebuild your self-worth

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:47.803
and your subconscious almost to,

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:50.530
to feel like you deserve better things.

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:51.660
I don't know if you know that's possible,

00:22:51.660 --> 00:22:52.687
but that's what.
- Yeah.

00:22:52.687 --> 00:22:54.380
- [Mark] That's the only hope I see.

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:55.213
- Yeah.

00:22:57.520 --> 00:22:58.640
- [Mark] What's the most painful thing

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:00.490
that you're escaping from, you think?

00:23:02.850 --> 00:23:03.890
- Memories. (chuckling)

00:23:03.890 --> 00:23:05.470
- [Mark] Of the like
sexual abuse or whatever?

00:23:05.470 --> 00:23:06.650
- Yeah, yeah.

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.270
Lots of just.
- [Mark] Just horrible.

00:23:08.270 --> 00:23:09.103
- Yeah.

00:23:10.088 --> 00:23:10.921
- [Mark] And what's the
most important lesson

00:23:10.921 --> 00:23:11.754
you've learned?

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:17.210
- It sounds cliche, but
not to judge people.

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:18.540
Like I-
- Mm-hm, that's a good one.

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:21.230
- Yeah, I just try to be
friendly to everyone I meet,

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:22.510
no matter what they're going through.

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:24.930
And I've met some really kind people

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:26.730
in some really bad situations.

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:31.730
And I wouldn't have, if I
weren't in this situation myself,

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:33.210
so I'm grateful for that too.

00:23:33.210 --> 00:23:34.710
That I've met some of these people.

00:23:34.710 --> 00:23:37.580
- [Mark] Yeah, do you feel
betrayed by your family or?

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:38.870
- In some ways, yeah.

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:40.820
Some, by some people, more than others.

00:23:42.460 --> 00:23:44.353
I don't feel angry at my family.

00:23:45.527 --> 00:23:46.360
I'm not angry at all.

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:50.060
Just, I think my parent figures,

00:23:50.060 --> 00:23:51.180
because when I say parent figures

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:53.060
I didn't just have my mom and dad.

00:23:53.060 --> 00:23:54.770
I have stepmom, stepdad.

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:58.310
You know, my dad's
girlfriends, many girlfriends.

00:23:58.310 --> 00:24:00.380
So I had a lot of
different parent figures,

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:01.770
coming in and out of my life.

00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:02.773
And I just,

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:07.000
I know I'm not grown yet
but as I'm older and I can,

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.220
you know, I feel more,

00:24:08.220 --> 00:24:10.740
I have that more motherly tent.

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:11.950
You know, those motherly tendencies.

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:15.510
I can't imagine putting
a kid through that,

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:17.160
like what me and my siblings went through.

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:20.490
I just don't understand how
a parent can like sit or eat,

00:24:20.490 --> 00:24:23.130
even if certain ones didn't inflict it,

00:24:23.130 --> 00:24:25.230
they watched it happen
or they let it happen.

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:26.960
And I just, that's really messed up

00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:30.170
and I don't know how it
could, how someone could.

00:24:30.170 --> 00:24:31.280
I'm not ready to forgive
them yet. (chuckling)

00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:33.370
- [Mark] Yeah, well, you
can break the cycle then.

00:24:33.370 --> 00:24:34.430
- I am.

00:24:34.430 --> 00:24:35.610
I hope.

00:24:35.610 --> 00:24:37.940
- [Mark] You still have
hope for your future?

00:24:37.940 --> 00:24:39.460
- I can't say.

00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:40.710
I wish I could say, yeah.

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.923
But a lot of times, no.

00:24:45.209 --> 00:24:46.663
I just want it to end.

00:24:49.854 --> 00:24:50.687
- All right Scarlett.

00:24:50.687 --> 00:24:51.920
Well, I wish you the best of luck.

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:53.240
I hope you figure out a way out of here.

00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:54.120
This is a dead end.

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:54.953
I mean, look around

00:24:54.953 --> 00:24:57.200
and look at the people
that are older than you.

00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:58.206
- Yeah, yeah.

00:24:58.206 --> 00:25:01.380
- [Mark] It's a hell of a
way to go with your life.

00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:02.590
- [Scarlett] It is.

00:25:02.590 --> 00:25:04.140
Thank you.
- [Mark] Thank you.

00:25:08.010 --> 00:25:09.067
That was great.

